tests/ui/check/err_show_parse.sky:3:9: error: expected a unit after `as`, found end of line
  |
3 | a = v as
  |         ^
  |       -- `as` shows a value in a unit
  = help: write the unit to show the value in, e.g. `v as km/h`

tests/ui/check/err_show_parse.sky:4:15: error: a value can be shown in only one unit
  |
4 | b = v as km/h as m
  |               ^^
  |     - the value
  |       ------- shown in this unit
  = help: remove the second `as`

tests/ui/check/err_show_parse.sky:5:15: error: `+` cannot follow `as`
  |
5 | c = v as km/h + 1
  |               ^
  |     - the value
  |       ------- shown in this unit
  = help: `as` shows a value in `km/h`; it does not produce a number to compute with. Put the arithmetic before it: `(… + …) as km/h`

tests/ui/check/err_show_parse.sky:6:10: error: expected a unit after `as`, found integer literal `5`
  |
6 | d = v as 5
  |          ^
  |       -- `as` shows a value in a unit
  = help: write the unit to show the value in, e.g. `v as km/h`

tests/ui/check/err_show_parse.sky:7:12: error: a unit's `/` cannot have spaces around it
  |
7 | e = v as m / s
  |            ^
  |          - unit so far
  = help: write the unit without spaces: `m/s`

tests/ui/check/err_show_parse.sky:8:17: error: `as` must come last in an expression
  |
8 | print(v as km/h if true else v)
  |                 ^^
  |       - the value
  |         ------- shown in this unit
  = help: to show a conditional in a unit, write `(a if c else b) as km` or `a if c else b as km`

tests/ui/check/err_show_parse.sky:9:1: error: expected an expression, found keyword `as`
  |
9 | as = 3
  | ^^
  = help: `as` follows a value: write `v as km/h` (it is also a reserved word, so it cannot name a variable)
